<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joseph Lane</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1801–1881</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joseph Lane was an American general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexican-american-war">Mexican–American War</a> and the first governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oregon-territory">Oregon Territory</a>, arriving in March 1849. He later represented Oregon in Congress and became one of its first US senators when it joined the Union in 1859. In 1860 he ran for vice-president with John C. Breckinridge on the Southern Democratic ticket.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joseph-lane.jpg" alt="Joseph Lane" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joseph_Lane_(cwpbh-02170).jpg: UnknownUnknown derivative work: Hic et nunc · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joseph_Lane_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
